5.2 Determination of protection measures
5.2.1 Measure Score




                                                         模
     In Model 1, we obtained a composite risk score 𝑅𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 of each region by analyzing 18
natural hazards. Next, in the above section, we quantified the value of the building to get the




                                                        学
score 𝑉𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 . By multiplying the risk score and the value score, 𝑀𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 is obtained, which is
used to assess the conservation priority of the building and the extent and scale of conservation
measures that need to be taken.




                                                      数
                                                                                             (30)
                                                   ：
     A higher 𝑀𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 indicates a higher value of the building, along with a higher risk of ex-




                                                  els
posure to natural hazards. Therefore, more urgent and comprehensive protection measures are
needed. Based on the statistical distribution of 𝑀𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 , we set reasonable thresholds to recog-
                           号
nize low, medium, and heigh grades, and the values of the specific thresholds need to be set



                                                od
based on expert recommendations and industry standards.
                          众


5.2.2 Score of Protection Measures
                                              Hm
    Low: For low-grade 𝑀𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 buildings, basic conservation measures, such as routine
                 公



maintenance and inspections and, where necessary, minor repairs, are undertaken. The risk or
value of these buildings is low, so the measures taken are mainly preventive and low-cost.
                                           AT
        信




    Medium: For medium-grade 𝑀𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 , moderate protection measures are implemented, in-
cluding enhanced structural inspections, improved safety features, and disaster preparedness
programs. These measures aim to increase the resistance and resilience of buildings and require
微

                                     M



moderate investment.
    High: For high-grade 𝑀𝑠𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑒 , implement comprehensive and high-intensity protection
                    ：




measures. This may include comprehensive structural reinforcement, installation of advanced
security systems, and customized risk management plans in cooperation with external experts.
Given the high risk or value of these buildings, the goal of the measures is to minimize potential
                   号




losses, even if this means higher initial costs.
     Note that: The "one-size-fits-all" approach to disaster protection measures ignores the im-
          信




pact of regional differences, architectural characteristics and socio-economic factors, and can
lead to poor protection and resource utilization. So specific protection measures still need to be
derived from a thoughtful local analysis by natural disaster experts.
  微




